speechtext:
The Laurentian Pilotage Authority advises as follows:
(a)	The tariffs in force for the years 1979, 1980 and 1981 were calculated and published to cover our expenses, without profit or loss. For purposes of publication of tariffs, we must use a marine traffic forecast and an estimate of expenses. Any discrepancy between our forecasts and reality necessarily results in a profit or a loss.
(b)	(i) In order to prevent repetition of a deficit, the authority was obliged to publish a second tariff in 1981. This tariff entered into force on September 1, 1981;
(ii)	The authority forecasts that 1982 revenues will be sufficient to cover operational and capital expenses;
(iii)	In each of the following years, a tariff will be published to ensure financial self-sufficiency.
